From: Stereolabs <embedded@stereolabs.com>
Subject: [PATCH] host1x-fence: drop dma_fence ref on FENCE_EXTRACT success path

dev_file_ioctl_fence_extract() takes a dma_fence reference via
sync_file_get_fence() but only releases it on the error paths
(put_fence:). The success path returns 0 without dma_fence_put(),
leaking one host1x_syncpt_fence (256B, kmalloc-256) per frame on the
Argus EGLStream thread (HOST1X_IOCTL_FENCE_EXTRACT). ~122 MB/h @ 60fps.
Ref: NVIDIA devforum 325399.
---
diff --git a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c
--- a/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c
+++ b/src/nvidia-oot/drivers/gpu/host1x-fence/dev.c
@@ -172,6 +172,7 @@
 		goto put_fence;
 	}
 
+	dma_fence_put(fence);
 	return 0;
 
 put_fence:
